 "customerTurns": 4,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Indesit dryer making a horrible squealing noise when it starts up, goes away after a few mins. Still dries fine"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is jockey / idler tension pulley. Can you tell me whether drum still turns?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yes, the drum still turns fine, and it heats and dries as normal. It's just the squeal for the first few minutes."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Coins, buttons, zips and hair grips are the usual cause. With the dryer unplugged, check the drum and its lifters, the lint filter and the slot it sits in, and turn the drum slowly while you listen. Did you find something (and have you removed it), can you see something stuck that won't come out, or is it all clear?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Nothing found in the door seal or filter. The drum turns by hand but feels a little rough with a slight squeak/scrape. Model is an Indesit IDC8T3B if that helps."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Run a short programme. Has the noise gone, or is it still there?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "It's still there, yes. Squeals for the first few minutes then quietens down. It's worse with a heavy load and on cold mornings, and doesn't happen every cycle."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: jockey / idler tension pulley]\nFrom what you have checked, this points to the jockey / idler tension pulley. An appliance engineer can confirm it and fit the part."
  }
 ],
